# Cross-surface feature parity

Lugin Chrome, Lugin Native, and Lugin Web share one product domain.

- Put generic collection, deck-building, tags, search, validation, formatting,
  copy coverage, bracket, import/export, and sync behavior in shared `src/`
  modules.
- A new or changed deck tag in `src/lib/deckTags.ts` must be available in all
  three clients. Do not create platform-specific tag catalogues or queries.
- When changing generic Collection or Deck behavior, inspect all three
  presentations and either expose it everywhere or document a concrete
  platform limitation.
- Keep React DOM and React Native presentation separate where appropriate;
  share the behavior rather than forcing shared UI components.
- Camera, scanner ML, SQLite, Binder, SecureStore, native filesystem, browser
  OAuth/storage, and platform permissions remain platform-specific.
- Before completion, test the shared rule and each affected client adapter.
